# ArtaQuest deploy-ignore — overrides Studio's SYNC_IGNORE_DEFAULTS.
#
# Studio CLI's push uses gitignore-style patterns from
# `SYNC_IGNORE_DEFAULTS` which includes `database` (intended to
# exclude the local SQLite `wp-content/database/` folder) and `cache`
# (intended to exclude transient caches).
#
# The `ignore` npm library matches case-insensitively against basename,
# so `database` ALSO silently excludes ANY directory named `Database`
# (capital D) anywhere in the tree — including the LMS PSR-4 namespace
# directory `wp-content/plugins/artaquest-lms/core/includes/Database/`
# and WooCommerce's `wp-content/plugins/woocommerce/src/Database/`.
# Same problem with `cache` matching PayPal SDK's `lib/PayPal/Cache/`.
#
# Re-include these directories so they actually reach production:
!wp-content/plugins/artaquest-lms/core/includes/Database
!wp-content/plugins/artaquest-lms/core/includes/Database/**
!wp-content/plugins/woocommerce/src/Database
!wp-content/plugins/woocommerce/src/Database/**
!wp-content/plugins/artaquest-lms/core/_core/libraries/paypal/includes/classes/vender/paypal/rest-api-sdk-php/lib/PayPal/Cache
!wp-content/plugins/artaquest-lms/core/_core/libraries/paypal/includes/classes/vender/paypal/rest-api-sdk-php/lib/PayPal/Cache/**
